{
  "abstract": "Unconditional Lean 4 formalization proving the lower bound C1a >= 13/10 = 1.30 for Terence Tao's Optimization Constant 1a (the Sidon-set autocorrelation constant C1a), improving on the previously known lower bounds 1.2748 (Matolcsi-Vinuesa 2010) and 1.292 (Piterbarg-Bajaj-Vincent 2026). The statement surface in Challenge.lean uses only canonical Mathlib and reproduces verbatim the L^2 definition of Constant1a.C1a from FormalConjectures (FormalConjectures/OptimizationConstants/1a.lean, commit 9097e2f90e66). The proof reduces an arbitrary nonnegative square-integrable function to a normalized density supported on [-1/4, 1/4], pairs its autoconvolution and autocorrelation against a 5-tent Bochner-admissible kernel mixture, applies symmetrized smoothing, a 66-mode cosine Bessel lower bound, and weighted Cauchy-Schwarz, and discharges the finite rational sinc^2 lower bounds, the integer Fejer-Riesz sum-of-squares certificate, and the closing quadratic inequalities inside Lean's kernel via decide +kernel using only standard axioms (propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice).",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Pavel Akhtyamov"
    }
  ],
